Subject: wasix: let an embedder choose the registered extensions

Extension namespaces were registered unconditionally: any guest under a
runtime built with an extension could import it, whatever the embedder
knew about the guest. Capabilities gains an extensions field - None
registers every extension the runtime carries, the default and what the
CLI does; a set registers only the listed namespaces, so a module that
imports anything else fails to instantiate exactly as it would on a
runtime without the extension. An embedder that runs declared packages
passes the declaration, and the linker becomes the enforcement: there
is no separate scan to drift from what actually links. The setting
rides the capabilities, so forked and exec'd children inherit it.

